# Soulmask server startup phases, for `cgprofile --log-match-file`.
#
# These are NOT invented for this tool. Every pattern below is lifted verbatim
# from the estate's own egg — game_stuff/soulmask/egg-soulmask-rcon-ksm-cgroups.json
# — so a phase boundary the profiler draws is the same boundary wings acts on:
#
#   WINGS_CG_PHASE_EVENTS  supplies the first three (informational, drives no
#                          cgroup behaviour, recorded to the Panel activity log)
#   config.startup.done    supplies "Create Dungeon Successed"
#   WINGS_CG_STEADY_MATCH  supplies the steady trigger — the line that ENDS the
#                          startup phase and makes wings apply the STEADY band
#
# That last one is why this file matters for a memory investigation: the moment
# it matches is the moment the server's cgroup limits change underneath it, so
# a step in the memory series either side of it is a different kind of event
# than one in the middle of a phase.
#
# Syntax is the egg's: `name=literal-substring`, or `name=regex:<regex>`.

steam-update-started=Checking for available updates
steam-update-done=regex:Success! App '3017300' (already up to date|fully installed)
world-load-begin=LogLoad: LoadMap:
dungeon-ready=Create Dungeon Successed
steady=registe server soulmask session succeed
